Step 5 Error:
Error: Failed to create/update resource
creating/updating Resource: PUT https://management.azure.com/.../virtualMachines/acctestVM-838250
RESPONSE 400: 400 Bad Request
ERROR CODE: InvalidParameter
The value of parameter imageReference.publisher is invalid.

Fix Process for Step 5:

Attempt 2:
- Problem Analysis: The module.replicator.body is missing publisher and offer fields in imageReference, only outputting sku and version. The module call has all 4 fields (publisher, offer, sku, version) but the module is not properly passing publisher and offer to the body output.
- Fix Method: Since I cannot modify the module, I need to override the body in azapi.tf to inject the missing fields. Use merge() to combine the module body with the correct imageReference. Must use HCL object (not JSON string) as AzAPI 2.0 requires HCL objects.
- Changes Made: 
  1. Added locals block with fixed_body that merges module.replicator.body with complete imageReference
  2. Modified azapi_resource.this to use local.fixed_body instead of module.replicator.body
- Result: Success - terraform apply completed successfully and idempotency verified

Final Result for Step 5: Fix successful. All steps completed successfully.
